You might be able to get by with a b!oLev if you use it in
the right place, but I wouldn't go without at least one
means of levitation. You must have left some boots in your
stash. You still have your MR, Reflection and Great AC. Your
unihorn is usually good enough to cure sickness and you
should start with a prayer available. You still have your
crystal ball to find the portals and plenty of food.
Removing curses is most important for your unihorn and your
BoH, oh, you don't have one of those! If the luckstone gets
cursed, just ditch it.

Often an experienced player will carry a second sack with a
few uncursing devices in it as a guard against the BoH being
cursed. The BoH can also be put in the emergency sack so it
won't be cursed. An emergency sack would have also been
handy in your situation, you'd at least have some seed holy
water.

I wouldn't tarry too long, the more you meet Rodney, the
more summoning storms and curses you'll have to deal with. I
would leave the amulet by the stairs just before I go back
down so I can use the Orb to level teleport and don't have
to worry about the amulet getting stolen while I'm
refitting.
